# Running tests

This project has PySide6 UI tests via `pytest-qt`. Without a Qt platform, `QApplication` aborts the whole pytest process (signal 6 / ABRT), which looks like a mysterious crash — not a normal test failure.

`tests/conftest.py` sets `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen` by default. Prefer:

```bash
.venv/bin/pytest tests/ -q --tb=short
```

If you override env or see Qt platform / ABRT / coredump on pytest, explicitly set:

```bash
QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen .venv/bin/pytest tests/ -q --tb=short
```

Do not treat a Qt abort as an application logic failure until the suite actually reports pass/fail under `offscreen`.
